---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---
<PageLayout title="Disclaimer" description="Stay Prepped provides general educational information about emergency preparedness. It is not medical, legal, financial or professional safety advice." updated={new Date('2026-10-24')}>
  <Callout type="safety" title="In an emergency">
    <p>If life is at risk, call 999. For urgent medical help that is not an emergency, call NHS 111. Always follow instructions from the emergency services and official sources.</p>
  </Callout>
  <h2>Educational information only</h2>
  <p>Everything on Stay Prepped, including guides, checklists and tool results, is general information to help you think about and plan for emergencies. It is not:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>medical or nutritional advice</li>
    <li>legal or financial advice</li>
    <li>a professional assessment of the risks to you, your home or your family</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Your circumstances may be different. Talk to a qualified professional about your situation, especially for babies, pregnancy, medical conditions, medicines and special diets.</p>
  <h2>Our tools give estimates</h2>
  <p>Our calculators use simple, stated assumptions to produce planning estimates. Real needs vary. Each tool page explains how it calculates its results so you can judge whether they suit you.</p>
  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>We take care to keep our content accurate and up to date, and each page shows when it was last reviewed. Official guidance can change, so check the official sources we link to.</p>
  <h2>Safety</h2>
  <p>Some activities described on this site, such as treating water or heating food without mains power, carry risks if done incorrectly. Follow manufacturers' instructions and official safety advice. Never use barbecues, camping stoves or generators indoors.</p>
</PageLayout>
